          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53488",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Host-root command execution via unvalidated image config labels in CRI plugin"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53488\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-53488](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53488**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.0.10, 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2|[CVE-2026-53488](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53488)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. In versions prior to 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10 the CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config (LABEL instruction in Dockerfile) to a container without validation. This may result in executing an arbitrary command on the host, via a plugin that consumes container labels for some operations. This issue has been fixed in versions 1.7.33, 2.3.2, 2.2.5, 2.1.9, and 2.0.10."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 8.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53489",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/containerd/containerd: containerd: Arbitrary host file read via symlink following in CRI checkpoint restore"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "containerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53489\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/containerd/containerd/v2\nFixed Version: 2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-53489](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489)\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53489**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/containerd/containerd/v2|2.1.9, 2.2.5, 2.3.2|[CVE-2026-53489](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53489)|\n\ncontainerd is an open-source container runtime. Versions prior to 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9 contain a bug where the CRI plugin restores container.log from a checkpoint image without validating a symlinked path. This could result in reading an arbitrary file on the host via kubectl logs. This issue has been fixed in versions 2.3.2, 2.2.5 and 2.1.9."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 7.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
